---
import Component from "../../../src/components/donate/MomentumNarrative.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for the NARRATIVE band in its `columns` layout — two columns of
// prose with the pull-quote card spanning beneath them, and no photo at all.
//
// The layout the other three narrative frames cannot show: `image-left`,
// `image-right` and `text-only` all answer "where does the picture go", and this
// one answers "what if there is no picture". It is also the proof that `columns`
// is an ADDITION — the sibling frames still render exactly as they did.
//
// `tinted` is set because that is how this band renders on /donate: it is the
// page's first narrative, and `tintedFlags` puts the first one on the tinted
// ground. It matters for more than accuracy — the pull quote is a WHITE card,
// which is invisible on an untinted white band, so a frame without it would
// show the quote as a bare crimson rule and misrepresent the design.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: MomentumNarrative-Columns</title>
    <style is:global>
      /* Two prose columns need a page-like width to be two columns at all; the
         fit-content wrapper would collapse them to one. */
      #codeyam-capture {
        width: 1200px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="codeyam-capture">
      <Component
        kicker="Why support Harvard Alumni in Tech?"
        title="We are at an important turning point."
        layout="columns"
        tinted
      >
        <p>
          We are a volunteer-led alumni community that has grown into a global network of founders,
          technologists, operators, investors, and professionals who are building, mentoring,
          launching, and opening doors for one another.
        </p>
        <p>
          To meet this moment, we need the infrastructure to support the momentum we are already
          seeing. That means more consistent programming, wider access to meaningful connections,
          stronger tools and resources for the volunteers who run it, and the operational foundation
          needed to serve our community at a higher level.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your support is what gives Harvard Alumni in Tech the ability to plan ahead rather than
          event to event, to invest more intentionally, and to create a stronger, more sustainable
          alumni-powered ecosystem.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now is the time to move from informal support to intentional investment. Together, we can
          create an impact that lasts beyond any one event, message, or moment.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            The future of this network will not be built by chance. It will be built by alumni who
            believe in what this community can become and choose to help power it forward.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </Component>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
